</section>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>System-level Comparison</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we evaluate the class-conditional image generation performance of GAE on the ImageNet benchmark. As summarized in Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Evaluation Metrics. ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, GAE establishes new SOTA results across multiple generative metrics while maintaining an extremely compact 32-dimensional latent space. Complementary analyses regarding reconstruction performance are provided in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Reconstruction Quality ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generative Performance.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When trained for 800 epochs, our framework attains a gFID of 1.31 without CFG and 1.13 with CFG. These results consistently surpass strong baselines such as FAE, which yields 1.48 and 1.29 respectively, and RAE, which achieves 1.51 and 1.13. Notably, while GAE matches the 1.13 gFID of RAE under guided sampling, RAE benefits from the more sophisticated AutoGuidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024</a>)</cite> protocol and larger model size. In contrast, our framework achieves comparable performance using only the standard CFG.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Efficiency and Convergence.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One of the most striking advantages of GAE is its remarkable training efficiency. Specifically, at only 80 epochs, GAE achieves a gFID of 1.82, which already surpasses the performance of VA-VAE trained for a full 800 epochs. This rapid convergence validates our core hypothesis that a semantically aligned latent space simplifies the learning objective for the subsequent diffusion model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Semantic-Reconstruction Trade-off.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Despite its focus on semantic alignment, GAE does not sacrifice visual fidelity. As illustrated in the Pareto Frontier (Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, left), GAE achieves a high LP accuracy of 69.4%, which is substantially higher than the 43.1% achieved by VA-VAE at the same latent dimension.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.10365v1/sigma.svg" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/307;" width="476" height="307"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Decoder stability against latent noise injection. We evaluate rFID by adding varying levels of Gaussian noise to the latent representations before decoding. The results demonstrate that models trained with higher <math id="S5.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> exhibit superior tolerance to latent distribution shifts, ensuring stable performance during generative sampling.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Reconstruction Stability</h3>

<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dynamic Noise Sampling.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Semantic-Reconstruction Trade-off. ‣ 5.1 System-level Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our analysis reveals a fundamental trade-off between reconstruction fidelity and generative performance governed by the noise strength <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. While minimizing <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> inherently yields superior rFID by reducing the perturbation of the latent manifold, it may fail to provide robust reconstruction performance as the noise level increases. Specifically, for the <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=32</annotation></semantics></math> configuration, although <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> maintains a slight lead in rFID during early training, this gap diminishes as the model scales, whereas <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> provides the necessary robustness to stabilize subsequent diffusion learning. In the <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=64</annotation></semantics></math> case, we observe that generative performance effectively plateaus between <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, we identify <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> for both <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=32</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=64</annotation></semantics></math> as the balanced configurations that harmonize semantic density with high-fidelity recovery, consistent with the experiment results in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis on Other Variants.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further extend our analysis to other autoencoder variants in Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Semantic-Reconstruction Trade-off. ‣ 5.1 System-level Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. RAE demonstrates exceptional reconstruction resilience, where its rFID remains remarkably stable even at a high perturbation level of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, which directly contributes to its superior gFID. In contrast, VTP exhibits a different behavior. While it achieves high semantic discriminability due to its training regime, its reconstruction performance is significantly more sensitive to latent perturbations. The sharp degradation in rFID hinders its generative performance, leading to sub-optimal gFID results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of standard deviation <math id="S5.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and latent dimension <math id="S5.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> on ImageNet-1K. gFID is reported without CFG. Autoencoders are trained on ImageNet-1K for 100 epochs.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Dim</td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><math id="S5.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">rFID <math id="S5.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">PSNR <math id="S5.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">LPIPS <math id="S5.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">SSIM <math id="S5.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">gFID <math id="S5.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S5.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.05</td>
