<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Reconstruction Quality</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a quantitative comparison of the reconstruction performance between our proposed GAE and various baseline models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Tab. <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix C Reconstruction Quality ‣ Geometric Autoencoder for Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, our model significantly outperforms traditional alignment-heavy frameworks such as RAE and FAE in terms of reconstruction fidelity. Specifically, at a 64-dimensional latent space, our method achieves a PSNR of 29.085 and an SSIM of 0.834, whereas RAE only yields 18.86 PSNR and 0.62 SSIM.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative comparison of reconstruction quality on ImageNet-1K. We compare our GAE with various generative and alignment-based methods across different latent dimensions (<math id="A3.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
